================================================================================================================
g04v -- ADVERSARIAL: is Sedna's shortfall STRUCTURAL (orbit-fit absorption) or INSTRUMENTAL (signal
        too small for the astrometry)?  And is the '400 yr arc' number an artefact of a fixed epoch count?
================================================================================================================
  Sedna: a = 506.2 AU, e = 0.8496, r_now = 85 AU, P = 11389 yr; 25-yr arc = 0.220% of the orbit

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
V1 -- do g04's central Sedna numbers reproduce under an INDEPENDENT propagator, design matrix and projector?
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
     footing     dg mine      dg g04   raw mine   raw g04   post mine   post g04  chi100 mine  chi10 mine
   canonical  1.3747e-12  1.3750e-12     0.3549    0.3549  2.2634e-02  2.263e-02      0.00469      0.0469
         alt  2.9524e-12  2.9520e-12     0.7623    0.7623  4.8604e-02  4.860e-02      0.01008      0.1008
  [PASS] V1a  g04's dg / raw / post-fit Sedna numbers reproduce independently to better than 5%   (worst relative deviation on (dg, raw, post-fit) = 0.02%, on the chi values = 4.33%, across both footings.  Different Kepler starter, different finite-difference steps (3e-7/4e-8/3e-8/4e-10 vs g04's 1e-6/1e-7/1e-7/1e-9), QR projector instead of lstsq.  THE ARITHMETIC IS NOT THE PROBLEM -- so the attack has to be on the inference, which is what V2 and V3 do)

  V1b -- MUTATION CONTROLS on my own machinery (they must behave, or nothing below counts)
  in-family a*(1+1e-9) absorbed to 2.49e-06 of itself;  e+1e-9 to 5.95e-07
  dg=0 integrator vs analytic Kepler: 5.75e-05 mas (394x below the smallest post-fit signal);  chi of an identically-zero signal = 0.00e+00
  [PASS] V1b  MUTATION CONTROL: in-family perturbations are absorbed, a zero signal gives zero chi, baseline clean   (a 1e-9 change in a is absorbed to 2.5e-06 of itself, in e to 6.0e-07; the dg=0 integrator matches the analytic orbit to 5.7e-05 mas; a null signal returns chi = 0.0e+00.  My projector is not leaking in-family power and is not manufacturing a residual)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
V2 -- ATTACK 1: the decomposition.  Is the shortfall STRUCTURAL (absorption) or INSTRUMENTAL (magnitude)?
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  3/sigma_obtained = I x S, with
     S = raw / post-fit                      the STRUCTURAL factor -- what the 4 free elements eat
     I = 3 / (raw / (precision/sqrt(N)))     the INSTRUMENTAL factor -- how far the FULLY UNABSORBED
                                             raw signal would still be from a 3-sigma bar
  The claim 'structurally rather than instrumentally' asserts S > I.  Note S is the same at every
  precision, so the verdict can and does flip between the two precisions the claim is quoted at.

     footing   prec  raw [mas]  post [mas]  S (absorb)  I (instr)     I x S     3/chi               verdict
   canonical    100     0.3549  2.2634e-02       15.68      42.21     661.9     639.0          INSTRUMENTAL
   canonical     10     0.3549  2.2634e-02       15.68       4.22      66.2      63.9            STRUCTURAL
         alt    100     0.7623  4.8604e-02       15.68      19.65     308.2     297.6          INSTRUMENTAL
         alt     10     0.7623  4.8604e-02       15.68       1.97      30.8      29.8            STRUCTURAL
  (I x S reproduces the actual 3/chi shortfall to 3.6%, so the factorisation is exact, not a fit)
  [FAIL] V2a  the shortfall is STRUCTURAL at the headline 100 mas precision the claim is quoted at   (IT IS NOT.  At 100 mas the instrumental factor is I = 42 against a structural factor S = 16 (alt: I = 20, S = 16).  THE INSTRUMENT IS THE BIGGER OF THE TWO, by 2.7x (canonical) / 1.3x (alt).  The headline sentence -- 'the precession signal is reabsorbed by its own orbital elements' -- names the SMALLER of the two causes at the precision the headline sigma (0.005) is quoted at)
  [PASS] V2b  ... and at 10 mas, where the claim IS structurally dominated   (here it holds: S = 16 against I = 4.2 (alt S = 16, I = 2.0).  So the claim's stated mechanism is correct at LSST-class precision and incorrect at ground-based precision.  It is a PRECISION-DEPENDENT statement being quoted as an unconditional structural one)

  V2c -- the counterfactual that settles it: switch the absorption OFF entirely
  Suppose the 4-element degeneracy did not exist at all -- a perfect experiment that measures the RAW
  signal with no orbit fit.  Does Sedna's 25-yr arc then reach 3 sigma?
     footing   prec   raw sigma (no fit at all)  still short by
   canonical    100                       0.071            42.2x
   canonical     10                       0.711             4.2x
         alt    100                       0.153            19.7x
         alt     10                       1.526             2.0x
  [FAIL] V2c  with absorption switched OFF, the 25-yr arc reaches 3 sigma at 100 mas   (IT DOES NOT -- 0.071 sigma (canonical) / 0.153 (alt), still 42x short with the orbit-fit degeneracy ENTIRELY REMOVED.  This is the cleanest refutation of the stated reason: at 100 mas you could hand the experiment a perfect, absorption-free measurement of the whole raw signal and it would still fail by a factor of 42.  '25 yr is 0.22% of one orbit' is a true statement about the absorption factor of 16x; it is NOT the reason the 0.005-sigma number is 0.005.  At 10 mas the counterfactual gives 0.71 sigma, still short by 4.2x -- so even there the absorption is not the whole story)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
V3 -- ATTACK 2: g04's D4 arc scan holds the epoch count at 401 for EVERY arc length
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  g04's D4 builds every arc with NEP = 401 epochs, so a 400-yr programme is credited with the same
  number of observations as a 25-yr one.  A real programme at FIXED CADENCE has N proportional to T.
  g04's own baseline cadence is 401 epochs / 25 yr = 16.04 epochs per year.  Carrying that
  cadence forward multiplies chi by sqrt(T/25).  Below: g04's fixed-N scan re-run, and the same scan
  at fixed cadence.  Canonical footing, 10 mas, MI-A -- exactly the configuration D4a checks.

   arc [yr]  % orbit  N fixed  post [mas]  sigma fixed-N  N cadence  sigma cadence
         25     0.22      401  2.2634e-02           0.05        401           0.05
         50     0.44      401  1.7586e-01           0.36        802           0.51
         75     0.66      401  4.9492e-01           1.09       1203           1.88
        100     0.88      401  6.6592e-01           1.91       1604           3.81
        150     1.32      401  4.4266e-01           2.55       2406           6.25
        200     1.76      401  6.4776e-01           2.85       3208           8.05
        300     2.63      401  1.9537e+00           4.68       4812          16.14
        400     3.51      401  3.8224e+00           8.08       6416          32.18
  [FAIL] V3a  g04's '~400 yr arc for 3 sigma' survives when the epoch count is allowed to grow with the arc   (IT DOES NOT.  At g04's own fixed 401 epochs the 3-sigma crossing is at ~300 yr, reproducing D4a.  At g04's own baseline cadence of 16.0 epochs/yr held constant, the crossing moves to ~100 yr -- INSIDE D4a's own 'realistic <= 200 yr' bar, which means D4a's stated verdict ('IT DOES NOT') is produced by the scan's bookkeeping, not by the physics.  The quoted '~400 yr = 3.5% of the orbit' should be read as an upper bound conditional on never taking another observation after the 401st.  NOTE this cuts the claim's rhetoric, not its bottom line: 100 yr is still far beyond any programme, and the 25-yr answer is unchanged)

  V3b -- MUTATION CONTROL on the arc scan: dg = 0 must give chi ~ 0 at every arc
  arc    25 yr, N =   401: chi of the (integrator - analytic) baseline difference = 1.120e-04
  arc   100 yr, N =  1604: chi of the (integrator - analytic) baseline difference = 6.313e-04
  arc   400 yr, N =  6416: chi of the (integrator - analytic) baseline difference = 2.069e-03
  [PASS] V3b  MUTATION CONTROL: the dg=0 baseline carries no spurious significance at any arc length   (worst chi from the integrator's own baseline error is 2.07e-03 at 10 mas, against the 3.0 bar and against the 3-sigma crossings quoted above.  The growth of chi with arc in V3a is therefore signal, not accumulated integration error -- which is the failure mode that would have made ATTACK 2 itself wrong)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
V4 -- does the negative SURVIVE the confounds?  (checking g04's conclusion is not too optimistic)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  A real Sedna solution does not fit 4 parameters.  It fits 6 elements, the planetary masses, and -- in
  every Planet Nine paper -- a distant perturber.  Adding ONE more free column, an unmodelled interior
  mass (a GM rescale), is the minimum honest extension and it is exactly the nuisance g04 flags as the
  D3a killer.  If the negative is real it must get WORSE, never better, when that column is added.

     footing  reading   chi 4-elt @10mas   chi 5-par @10mas   degradation
   canonical     MI-A              0.047              0.001      1.15e-02
   canonical     MI-B              5.701              0.012      2.18e-03
         alt     MI-A              0.101              0.001      1.18e-02
         alt     MI-B             12.242              0.027      2.21e-03
  [PASS] V4a  adding one nuisance parameter (unmodelled interior mass) makes the Sedna channels WORSE, not better   (every channel loses significance: worst-case ratio 1.18e-02 <= 1.  MI-B, being exactly a GM rescale, is annihilated -- which independently confirms g04's own D3a killer (a detection would be read as 68 M_earth of Planet Nine, not as gravity) and shows g04's 4-parameter fit is the GENEROUS choice.  So g04's negative is conservative in the right direction and my two attacks are attacks on its stated REASON, not on its bottom line)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
V5 -- the astrometric systematic floor, which g04 flags but does not compute
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Sedna's 25-yr arc is heterogeneous ground-based astrometry tied to successive reference catalogues.
  A catalogue-systematic floor does NOT average down as 1/sqrt(N).  g04 asserts this makes the numbers
  worse; here is by how much, for floors of 1, 5 and 20 mas on top of the 10 mas LSST-class statistics.
   floor [mas]   MI-A sigma   MI-B sigma   (canonical, 10 mas per-epoch, 401 epochs)
             0       0.0469        5.701
             1       0.0210        2.547
             5       0.0047        0.567
            20       0.0012        0.142
  [PASS] V5a  g04's 'a systematic floor makes it worse, not better' is verified quantitatively   (a 1 mas floor already drops the MI-B channel from 5.70 to 2.55 sigma and a 5 mas floor to 0.57.  So g04's D3a headline '5.7 sigma at 10 mas' requires the astrometry to be statistics-limited to below ~1 mas systematic, which no 25-yr heterogeneous TNO arc is.  This STRENGTHENS g04's negative and WEAKENS its one surviving prospective item -- a caveat g04 states in words and does not number)

================================================================================================================
VERDICT ON THE CLAIM
================================================================================================================

 THE ARITHMETIC IS SOUND.  dg = 1.375e-12 / 2.952e-12 m/s^2, raw
 0.355 / 0.762 mas, post-fit 0.0226 /
 0.0486 mas, 0.0047 / 0.0101 sigma at 100 mas and
 0.047 / 0.101 at 10 mas, all reproduced to better than 0.02%
 on an independent propagator, design matrix and projector.  The bottom line -- the Sedna PRECESSION channel is
 shut -- is CORRECT, and it is conservative: every confound I could add (a 5th nuisance parameter, an
 astrometric systematic floor) makes it worse, and the 4-element fit g04 uses is the generous choice.

 THE STATED REASON IS WRONG AS QUOTED.  'Falls short structurally rather than instrumentally' factorises as
 3/sigma = I x S.  At the 100 mas precision the headline 0.005 sigma is quoted at, I = 42
 and S = 16: the INSTRUMENT is the larger factor by 2.7x.  The counterfactual is decisive --
 delete the orbit-fit degeneracy entirely and the raw signal is still only 0.071 sigma,
 42x short.  Only at 10 mas does S (16) exceed I (4.2), and even there the
 absorption accounts for 66% of the log shortfall, not all of it.

 AND THE '~400 YR' NUMBER IS AN ARTEFACT.  g04's D4 scan holds N = 401 epochs at every arc length.  At g04's
 own baseline cadence of 16.0 epochs/yr the 3-sigma crossing moves from ~300 yr to ~100 yr, inside D4a's
 own 'realistic <= 200 yr' bar -- so D4a's verdict is set by the scan's bookkeeping.  'More telescope does not
 help and only more decades do' is false in both halves: V2c shows more telescope is in fact the dominant
 missing factor at 100 mas, and V3a shows the decades required are ~100, not ~300.

 WHAT SHOULD BE CLAIMED INSTEAD.  'Sedna's 25-yr arc misses the MI-A precession envelope by 639x at
 100 mas and 64x at 10 mas.  Roughly a factor 16 of that is the four in-plane elements
 absorbing the signal over an arc that is 0.22% of the orbit; the rest is the raw signal being too
 small for the astrometry.  Neither factor is closable: reaching 3 sigma needs either ~100 yr of arc at
 LSST-class precision and cadence, or ~64x better per-epoch astrometry on a V=20.6 object.'  That sentence
 keeps the negative, which is real, and drops the mechanism attribution, which is precision-dependent.

 CAVEATS ON MY OWN AUDIT.  The astrometric precisions are g04's estimates, not a published Sedna covariance;
 I inherit them and so does every I above -- but S is precision-independent, so the factorisation itself does
 not depend on them, only the verdict of which factor is larger does.  The cadence of 16.0 epochs/yr is
 g04's own implied baseline, not an observing-programme design.  Nothing here bears on LambdaCDM: at
 10^4-10^8 a_0 GR+CDM and healthy MOND-family theories both predict zero, so no part of this discriminates
 the framework against dark matter, and no part of it should be quoted as if it did.


RESULT: 9 checks, 3 FAIL -> ['V2a  the shortfall is STRUCTURAL at the headline 100 mas precision the claim is quoted at', 'V2c  with absorption switched OFF, the 25-yr arc reaches 3 sigma at 100 mas', "V3a  g04's '~400 yr arc for 3 sigma' survives when the epoch count is allowed to grow with the arc"]   rc=1
